.\" Process this file with
.\" groff -man -Tascii lpt.4
.\"
.TH LPT 4 "March 2026" "Substrate Kernel" "Device Drivers Manual"
.SH NAME
lpt \- ISA parallel ports
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B /dev/comm/parallel0
.br
.B /dev/comm/parallel1
.br
.B /dev/comm/parallel2
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B lpt
driver exposes detected ISA-compatible parallel ports under
.BR /dev/comm/parallel0
through
.BR /dev/comm/parallel2 .
These map to LPT1 through LPT3 respectively.
.PP
Substrate does not publish parallel device nodes for ports that do not appear
to exist. The driver relies on ISA legacy discovery before registering
.B /dev/comm/parallel*
nodes.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /dev/comm/parallel0
LPT1, if present.
.TP
.B /dev/comm/parallel1
LPT2, if present.
.TP
.B /dev/comm/parallel2
LPT3, if present.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR intro (4),
.BR isa (9)
